  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-07-25T07:51:53.155Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The current detection method for whether or not to go into hand tracking mode seems rather unreliable. Using Virtual Desktop is seems to think that I am always using hand tracking and it makes the controllers barely usable. Meanwhile, using ALVR with hand tracking I can move my fingers perfectly well, but it still thinks I'm just holding controllers and doesn't enable any of the pinch controls.\n\n**Settings for Virtual Desktop:**\n\n*Streaming > Advanced Options:*\n\n- ✅ Forward Tracking Data\n\n- ❌ Emulate Vive Trackers\n\n- ❌ Emulate Index Controllers\n\n**Settings for ALVR (20.9.1):**\n\n*Headset > Controllers:*\n\n- ✅ Tracked\n\n- ✅ Enable Skeleton\n\n- ❌ Gestures\n\nPerhaps the best solution would be a manual override in the settings to engage/disengage hand-tracking mode.",
